  <h2>Use tags without exposing plans or pressuring agreement</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to confirm a real employer, coworker, client, family member, relationship, travel plan, address, appointment, payment, password, contract, health detail, schedule, or private disagreement. Use Lena, Marcus, Eli, Cedar House, and the fictional event board. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Verified details:</b> Choose three confirmed fictional facts. State each with an accurate tag and a cooperative falling voice.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Open checks:</b> Choose three blank or uncertain tasks. Use rising tags and accept either confirmation or correction.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Grammar range:</b> Include <span class="ex">be</span>, Present Perfect, a modal, Present or Past Simple, one negative-meaning word, and one special pattern.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Respect:</b> Replace one tag that embeds a preferred answer with a neutral full question. Respond to every answer rather than repeating the pressure.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: run a 75–90 second fictional coordination check</h3>
    <p>Use a supplied event board with four confirmed details, three blank tasks, and one incorrect assumption. Produce at least six tags using four operator systems. Include one negative statement, one negative-meaning word, one special pattern, one expected-agreement fall, and one open-check rise. Your partner must confirm at least two assumptions and correct at least one. Finish by changing one potentially pressuring tag into a neutral full question.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener recover the statement operator, polarity, subject reference, truth of every short answer, intended checking job, and whether the voice movement invites alignment or leaves room for correction?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You matched perfect have, reversed negative-meaning nobody, and interpreted a correcting positive short answer from its full statement.">
