  <h2>Reflect: what did the speaker assume, and what may the listener correct?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">I find the operator by...</span> <span class="ex">I reverse the polarity by...</span> <span class="ex">A negative-meaning word takes...</span> <span class="ex">A short answer responds to...</span> <span class="ex">A falling tag often...</span> <span class="ex">I choose a full question when...</span></p>
    <p>Take one fictional event fact and produce three versions: a neutral full question, an open rising tag, and an expected-agreement falling tag. Explain how the grammar stays stable while the social stance changes.</p>
